0|Hello everyone!|
1|Welcome to The Cozy French,|
2|your little get-together|
3|to learn French through|
4|natural, warm conversations.|
5|I'm Léa, and I'm very happy|e=coeur
6|to be with you again today.|
7|And I'm Mathieu!|
8|Hello, dear friends!|
9|Whether you're at home,|
10|on public transport|
11|or making your coffee,|
12|make yourselves comfortable.|
13|We're delighted to spend this time with you.|
14|Mathieu, today I'd like to start|
15|with a question.|
16|When you were a child,|
17|what job did you want to do later?|
18|Ah!|e=surpris
19|You really want to know my childhood dreams?|
20|Of course! Why the hesitation?|
21|Because I changed my mind so many times|
22|that my family didn't know what to think.|
23|At six, I wanted to be a firefighter.|
24|At eight, an explorer.|
25|And at ten, a chef.|
26|A chef? That doesn't surprise me,|e=rire
27|given your love of food!|i=repas:la nourriture
28|Exactly!|
29|But I thought a chef mostly spent|
30|his time tasting delicious dishes.|
31|You forgot that you also|
32|had to cook them!|
33|Yes. When my mum explained|
34|that you had to work for hours,|
35|clean and organise a kitchen,|
36|my enthusiasm dropped a little.|e=gene
37|And today, do you still like cooking?|
38|Yes, but calmly at home,|
39|without twenty customers waiting for dinner.|
40|What about you, Léa? What was your dream?|
41|For a long time,|
42|I wanted to be a vet.|
43|I loved animals and I dreamed|
44|of caring for every cat in the neighbourhood.|e=coeur
45|Every cat?|
46|Your parents must have been thrilled!|e=rire
47|Not really!|
48|But as I grew up, I understood|
49|that this job required|
50|a lot of scientific knowledge|
51|and that sometimes you had|
52|to go through difficult situations.|
53|So you changed your mind.|
54|Yes. But I kept something from that dream:|
55|the wish to help and understand others.|
56|That's interesting. The job changed,|e=idee
57|but part of your dream stayed.|
58|Exactly.|
59|And that's precisely our topic today:|
60|"What's Your Dream Job?",|
61|in other words,|
62|"What is the job of your dreams?"|
63|A very simple question when you're a child,|
64|but much more complicated|
65|when you become an adult.|
66|Because you have to think about our passions,|
67|our skills, our financial situation|
68|and sometimes our family's expectations.|
69|Not to mention an important question:|
70|would we really enjoy this job|
71|every single day?|
72|Today, we're going to talk about all that,|
73|with stories|
74|and useful French expressions|
75|to talk about work and the future.|i=travail:le travail
76|And if you're learning French,|
77|just listen calmly.|
78|No need to understand every word.|
79|Just try to follow our conversation.|
80|Before we start, tell us|
81|in the comments:|
82|what job did you dream of doing|
83|when you were a child?|
84|And has your dream changed since then?|
85|Now, let's begin!|
86|So, Mathieu,|
87|why did you want to be an explorer?|
88|I think I mostly loved adventure.|i=voyage:l'aventure
89|I wanted to discover new places,|
90|meet people|
91|and see extraordinary things.|
92|So what you really liked|e=idee
93|was discovery.|
94|Exactly.|
95|I hadn't thought about the job's difficulties.|
96|And why did you want to be a firefighter?|
97|Because I admired brave people|
98|who come to help others.|
99|There you go. Behind your dreams,|B={"mode":"mindmap","bg":"craie","word":"les valeurs","items":["la curiosité","l'aventure","l'envie d'être utile"]}
100|there were certain values:|
101|curiosity, adventure and the wish to be useful.|
102|You know, I'd never looked at|
103|my childhood dreams that way.|BE
104|And yet they can help us understand|
105|what still interests us today.|
106|For example, someone who wanted to be a pilot|
107|because they loved travelling|
108|could end up working in tourism.|
109|Exactly. Or someone|
110|who dreamed of being a teacher|
111|might discover that they mostly love|
112|explaining things|
113|and choose another job in training.|
114|So our dreams can evolve|
115|without disappearing completely.|
116|Yes. But we also have to accept|
117|that a passion won't necessarily become|
118|our profession.|
119|Ah, that's important.|e=idee
120|I love taking photos|
121|during my walks,|i=nature:mes promenades
122|but I'm not sure I'd like having to|
123|photograph events every weekend.|
124|Exactly. Loving an activity freely|
125|isn't always the same thing|
126|as having to do it to earn a living.|
127|You know, I have a friend who loved drawing|
128|when she was a teenager.|
129|She wanted to be an illustrator.|
130|And today?|
131|She works in teaching,|i=etudes:l'enseignement
132|but she still draws in the evening.|
